    // Winter wind: each month's factor is the cube of the monthly mean wind
    // speed at 10 m (the power-density relation) averaged over Moscow,
    // Novosibirsk and Anapa (Weather Spark, "Climate and Average Weather Year
    // Round in Russia", table "Average Wind Speed in Russia", read
    // 2026-10-25: Moscow 11.9, 11.7, 10.8, 9.8, 9.3, 8.6, 8.0, 8.5, 9.5, 10.5,
    // 11.0 and 11.7 mph; Novosibirsk 12.2, 12.0, 12.0, 11.6, 10.6, 8.7, 7.8,
    // 8.4, 9.7, 11.2, 12.2 and 12.7; Anapa 13.5, 13.7, 12.6, 10.6, 9.2, 9.0,
    // 9.6, 10.1, 10.6, 11.7, 12.8 and 13.4), over its year mean, times the
    // Eastern Interconnection's annual mean factor, 0.567 (authoring scale,
    // as in the other Plan 7 files; the cube law is an authoring judgment).
    // It peaks from November to February.
