    // Unit sizes and operating parameters follow the North American catalog
    // (spec section 3.2), except where a row names a local unit: coal is a
    // 230 MW unit, as at Kharanorskaya [P7-IPS-004], so its start-up cost
    // and ramp are scaled per MW (ruling 24). The CCGT row's project mixes a
    // 235 MW and two 160 MW units [P7-IPS-006] (Kommersant, read 2026-10-25),
    // so no single local CCGT size is sourced and the catalog keeps 500 MW.
    // Money and build months come from the Plan 7 research note by its
    // pacing method (ratios from its pacing table, at full precision; game
    // values rounded to 3 significant figures per kW, per kW-year or per
    // MWh, then multiplied by capacity; monthly fixed O&M is the
    // per-kW-year value x kW / 12, to the nearest rouble). The note has no
    // IPS/UPS fixed O&M row, so every kind's fixed O&M follows ruling 4
    // (authoring judgment: derived from its capital row by NA kind
    // relativity). The nuclear and hydro capital rows are the General
    // Scheme's investment over planned additions, which include VAT and
    // forecast prices of each year. Gas is the regulated FAS wholesale price
    // [P7-IPS-011], priced on its 7,900 kcal/m3 basis (33.080 GJ per 1,000
    // m3) and applied to the S&L heat rates without a calorific-basis
    // conversion (pacing judgment: the note has no conversion row), and fuel
    // only: the local marginal has no variable O&M row. Coal and nuclear
    // have no fuel row, so they follow ruling 19 (authoring judgment: no
    // sourced local fuel row): the North American game marginal x the local
    // reference tariff over the NA one, 5,803.835 / 100 = 58.03835, a
    // price-level proxy from [P7-IPS-001]. Start-ups follow ruling 2 (NA
    // start-up x local marginal / NA marginal, at full precision).
    catalog: [
