    // Climate 2, southern Russia and the Caucasus (Rostov-on-Don, Krasnodar,
    // Volgograd, Baku and Tbilisi): a milder winter and an air-conditioned
    // summer afternoon. Climate 3, the Urals, Siberia, northern Kazakhstan
    // and Murmansk: the deepest winter. Climate 4, Central Asia (Almaty,
    // Shymkent, Tashkent, Dushanbe and Bishkek): a winter evening peak and an
    // air-conditioned summer afternoon (spec section 28.6). The hourly
    // shapes, the month-to-shape assignment and the monthly factors are
